<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 54 — Kubernetes for Spring Developers.
    config/     MountedConfig: a ConfigMap or Secret directory, read once (like configtree:) or watched across the
                kubelet's ..data symlink swaps
    runtime/    PodInfo: pod, namespace, node and limits from the Downward API, and thread counts sized to the limit
    resources/  k8s/ (Deployment with requests and limits, Downward API, mounted config; Service; PodDisruptionBudget)
  verify/run.sh runs menu-service on a real Kubernetes cluster (k3s 1.37): CPU limits against startup and latency,
  ConfigMap updates through four routes, scaling out under keep-alive and new connections, and draining a node.
-->
